And your biology training gives us an important Reality Stitch: in cells, the plasma membrane is usually the selectively gated information/material boundary; a cell wall, where present, is generally an extracellular structural layer that is much more porous. Plants, fungi, and many prokaryotes have walls; animal cells don’t.

The biological machinery is almost embarrassingly Pantheon-shaped:

\boxed{
\text{Outside}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Membrane}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Inside}
}

But the membrane isn’t merely a barrier. It contains typed gates:

\begin{aligned}
\text{channel} &\rightarrow \text{selective passage}\\
\text{carrier} &\rightarrow \text{bind + transform configuration}\\
\text{pump} &\rightarrow \text{spend energy to create/maintain gradient}\\
\text{receptor} &\rightarrow \text{signal crosses without molecule crossing}\\
\text{vesicle} &\rightarrow \text{package crosses boundary}\\
\text{junction} &\rightarrow \text{direct cell-to-cell route}
\end{aligned}

And that last distinction is huge:

\boxed{\text{information can cross a boundary without its carrier crossing}}

A ligand can remain outside, bind a receptor, and trigger a cascade inside.

That’s practically a biological cameo.

The external object appears at the boundary; the inside reconstructs an enormous consequence from a tiny recognized reference:

L_{\text{outside}}
\rightarrow
R_{\text{membrane}}
\rightarrow
\text{second messengers}
\rightarrow
\text{gene expression / metabolism / behavior}.

Small appearance, enormous reconstruction.

Meanwhile secretion is almost fourth-wall-like in the opposite direction:

\text{inside state}
\rightarrow
\text{secreted signal}
\rightarrow
\text{outside world}
\rightarrow
\text{other cells}.

So our Semantic Circulatory System gets a more general parent abstraction:

\boxed{\textbf{Boundary Physiology}}

Study a boundary by asking:

What crosses? What doesn’t? What merely signals across? What requires energy? What follows a gradient? What establishes the gradient? What recognizes the cargo? What transforms during passage? What gets packaged? What leaks?

Now apply that to language, interfaces, minds, AI systems, organizations, nations, stories, APIs—

same questions, different renderer.

And cell walls give us another beautiful variant. Plant cells can be connected through plasmodesmata, channels traversing the wall and linking neighboring cytoplasms. So two apparently separate bounded units can possess carefully controlled cross-wall continuity.

That suggests:

\boxed{
\textbf{Semantic Plasmodesmata}
=
\text{persistent narrow channels joining otherwise separately governed representational spaces}
}

